(221595, 12761, 5475, '<td valign="top">This is my only 10 so far.  So many people think that a flower, if properly exposed and in focus, makes a wonderful image.  That is not true, and in many cases, it is the lighting that sets a great floral image apart from the nice, but boring images.  This shot is nearly perfect in lighting, which is so tough to achieve.  The range from light to dark tones is very good, without any lown highlights.  The lower dark petals offset the bright upper petals in a way that balances your composition.  The actual shape of your composition is nothing special, but the lighting really makes it!  DOF is great, focus is perfect, lighting is great.  the only thing I can find fault in are the two white specks on the left side of the image (in the black background).  That''s easy to fix for printing, and I won''t count off for it due to the restriction on spot editing (this image is a good reason to get rid of that rule).  Nice shot, my only 10 so far!  Good luck in the challenge!<br/>JD Anderson</td>', 'This is my only 10 so far.  So many people think that a flower, if properly exposed and in focus, makes a wonderful image.  That is not true, and in many cases, it is the lighting that sets a great floral image apart from the nice, but boring images.  This shot is nearly perfect in lighting, which is so tough to achieve.  The range from light to dark tones is very good, without any lown highlights.  The lower dark petals offset the bright upper petals in a way that balances your composition.  The actual shape of your composition is nothing special, but the lighting really makes it!  DOF is great, focus is perfect, lighting is great.  the only thing I can find fault in are the two white specks on the left side of the image (in the black background).  That''s easy to fix for printing, and I won''t count off for it due to the restriction on spot editing (this image is a good reason to get rid of that rule).  Nice shot, my only 10 so far!  Good luck in the challenge!JD Anderson', '2003-02-23 13:01:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(221596, 12610, 2178, '<td valign="top">Cool concept, but slightly overexposed.</td>', 'Cool concept, but slightly overexposed.', '2003-02-23 13:02:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(221597, 12414, 2178, '<td valign="top">Nice and vibrant. DOF  properly shows  the bee as your subject allowing the flower to provide great color .</td>', 'Nice and vibrant. DOF  properly shows  the bee as your subject allowing the flower to provide great color .', '2003-02-23 13:06:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(221598, 12533, 2178, '<td valign="top">Nice tight shot, the skin tones are a tad overexposed though.</td>', 'Nice tight shot, the skin tones are a tad overexposed though.', '2003-02-23 13:07:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(221599, 12490, 5475, '<td valign="top">So how cool is this shot?  Enought o get a 10 from me!!  I love the lighting on this!  I''d be interested to find out what your lighting setup was like.  The brighter yellow circle of light around the center of the flower is great!  THe lower part of that brighter yellow is a little bit blown out, but not enough to complain about.  Cropping on the yellow flower is perfect, too.  I really like the composition created with that crop.  For the most part, your background provides added interest without being a distraction.  I like that the background is not all solid black.  With that said, I do think the small amount of background ''leafs'' that are overlapping the yellow petals is distracting.  I would have moved those behind the flower.  Better yet, I would have trimmed them out of the picture.  The lighting on the background elements works very well, but these leaves in particular have the same lighting as the yellow flower.  They are not part of the flower, but the lighting on them is too strong for them to match with the background elements.  OK...  I feel like I am rambling!  Even though I found something I would have changed in this image, I am still giving it a 10 because it has enough WOW factor to overcome the small flaws!  Nice work!<br/>JD Anderson</td>', 'So how cool is this shot?  Enought o get a 10 from me!!  I love the lighting on this!  I''d be interested to find out what your lighting setup was like.  The brighter yellow circle of light around the center of the flower is great!  THe lower part of that brighter yellow is a little bit blown out, but not enough to complain about.  Cropping on the yellow flower is perfect, too.  I really like the composition created with that crop.  For the most part, your background provides added interest without being a distraction.  I like that the background is not all solid black.  With that said, I do think the small amount of background ''leafs'' that are overlapping the yellow petals is distracting.  I would have moved those behind the flower.  Better yet, I would have trimmed them out of the picture.  The lighting on the background elements works very well, but these leaves in particular have the same lighting as the yellow flower.  They are not part of the flower, but the lighting on them is too strong for them to match with the background elements.  OK...  I feel like I am rambling!  Even though I found something I would have changed in this image, I am still giving it a 10 because it has enough WOW factor to overcome the small flaws!  Nice work!JD Anderson', '2003-02-23 13:08:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(221600, 12712, 2178, '<td valign="top">Great shot, nice composition and good focus. Nice dramatic lighting too.</td>', 'Great shot, nice composition and good focus. Nice dramatic lighting too.', '2003-02-23 13:09:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(221601, 12379, 5475, '<td valign="top">This is a very simple, but very effective image.  I like the shapes and the lighting is very fun.  I''d be interested to see the original file to see how much post processing was required to get this version.  Nicely done...  9<br/>JD Anderson</td>', 'This is a very simple, but very effective image.  I like the shapes and the lighting is very fun.  I''d be interested to see the original file to see how much post processing was required to get this version.  Nicely done...  9JD Anderson', '2003-02-23 13:09:53.000000', NULL, 1),
