(223825, 12414, 5507, '<td valign="top">Great shot!Good detail on Bee! 10</td>', 'Great shot!Good detail on Bee! 10', '2003-02-25 04:42:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(223828, 12352, 1169, '<td valign="top">This is a picture of a lego head<br/>It has been distorted with a magnifying glass<br/>The red patches are just there when i increased the contrast.<br/> <br/>Thanks to everyone who commented</td>', 'This is a picture of a lego headIt has been distorted with a magnifying glassThe red patches are just there when i increased the contrast. Thanks to everyone who commented', '2003-02-25 04:47:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(223893, 12491, 1143, '<td valign="top">Hey! Cool. I didn''t expect to place, but I won''t complain. Low scoring challenges can be nice ;)<br/>I''ve seen a lot of really nice flower shots on photosig, and then magnetic''s cliche shot inspired me to try one myself.  The shot has actually been rotated 90 degrees cc, so the light was to my right instead of above. I used a small halogen work light from home depot with a homemade diffuser in front (frame covered with white cloth from walmart). <br/>I adjusted levels some in photoshop - especially the black - until I got what I wanted, and sharpened just a bit. I had an alternate version with more light on the stem, but I prefer this one. I think it''s more dramatic to have the stem disappearing into the black. However, I didn''t take into account that some people don''t have their monitors calibrated correctly and wouldn''t be able to see it at all. Live and learn. Thanks for the comments!</td>', 'Hey! Cool. I didn''t expect to place, but I won''t complain. Low scoring challenges can be nice ;)I''ve seen a lot of really nice flower shots on photosig, and then magnetic''s cliche shot inspired me to try one myself.  The shot has actually been rotated 90 degrees cc, so the light was to my right instead of above. I used a small halogen work light from home depot with a homemade diffuser in front (frame covered with white cloth from walmart). I adjusted levels some in photoshop - especially the black - until I got what I wanted, and sharpened just a bit. I had an alternate version with more light on the stem, but I prefer this one. I think it''s more dramatic to have the stem disappearing into the black. However, I didn''t take into account that some people don''t have their monitors calibrated correctly and wouldn''t be able to see it at all. Live and learn. Thanks for the comments!', '2003-02-25 07:30:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(224117, 12421, 6349, '<td valign="top">had to come back to this and tell you that I added it to my favorites.  This was my highest scoring 10 this week and its at 45?!  Well, off to check the others!  Great job.</td>', 'had to come back to this and tell you that I added it to my favorites.  This was my highest scoring 10 this week and its at 45?!  Well, off to check the others!  Great job.', '2003-02-25 12:46:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(224123, 12561, 6349, '<td valign="top">I''m back here again to let you know this was one of 4 of my tens this week and I''m very surprised to see it placed so low.  I marked it as one of my favorites and I''d gladly trash half of the photos that beat you.  Great job.</td>', 'I''m back here again to let you know this was one of 4 of my tens this week and I''m very surprised to see it placed so low.  I marked it as one of my favorites and I''d gladly trash half of the photos that beat you.  Great job.', '2003-02-25 12:50:15.000000', NULL, 0),
